# nonlinear.mienlo -- chi(2)/chi(3)/EO/saturable-absorber registry (plain CSV;
# full-line '#' comments are allowed in THIS registry and skipped by
# optprops.load_nonlinear).
#
# One 'kind' column discriminates row types; unused columns stay blank:
#   kind=chi2_tensor : crystal point_group d_il_pm_V kleinman lam_ref_nm
#   kind=chi2_process: crystal process lam_pump_nm theta_deg phi_deg d_eff_pm_V
#   kind=pockels     : crystal r_coeffs_pm_V geometry
#   kind=n2          : material n2_m2_W lam_ref_nm
#   kind=saturable   : I_sat_W_cm2 T0 tau_recovery_s
#
# d_il_pm_V packing: the full 3x6 contracted (Voigt) d-matrix, ROW-MAJOR,
# rows i=1..3 (polarization component) separated by '|', each row exactly six
# ';'-separated floats l=1..6 (11->1, 22->2, 33->3, 23/32->4, 13/31->5,
# 12/21->6), in pm/V, in the CRYSTAL principal frame:
#   d11;d12;d13;d14;d15;d16|d21;...;d26|d31;...;d36
# Signs: relative signs within a row set follow the point-group matrix form
# (see notes); absolute sign conventions across the literature are not pinned.
# 'crystal' must name a birefringence/uniaxial.miebrf or biaxial.mibiax row.
# 'material' (n2 rows) names a materials.miemat row, resolved LAZILY by the
# consumer (staged rows may precede their materials row -- see notes on yag).
# 'r_coeffs_pm_V': named ';'-packed pairs, e.g. "r33=30.8;r13=8.6".
kind,name,crystal,point_group,d_il_pm_V,kleinman,lam_ref_nm,process,lam_pump_nm,theta_deg,phi_deg,d_eff_pm_V,r_coeffs_pm_V,geometry,material,n2_m2_W,I_sat_W_cm2,T0,tau_recovery_s,reference,notes
chi2_tensor,linbo3_d,linbo3,3m,0;0;0;0;4.6;-3.1|-3.1;3.1;0;4.6;0;0|4.6;4.6;25.2;0;0;0,true,1064,,,,,,,,,,,,,"Shoji, Kondo, Kitamoto, Shirane & Ito, J. Opt. Soc. Am. B 14, 2268 (1997) (d33=25.2, d31~4.6, Eckardt-scale); d22=3.1 Choy & Byer 1976 lineage (Boyd-era tables)","3m matrix [[0,0,0,0,d15,-d22],[-d22,d22,0,d24,0,0],[d31,d31,d33,0,0,0]], Kleinman d15=d24=d31; magnitudes on the modern Eckardt/Shoji absolute scale (legacy d33=34.4 runs ~25-30% high); relative sign of d22 vs d31/d33 not pinned"
chi2_tensor,bbo_d,bbo,3m,0;0;0;0;0.08;-2.2|-2.2;2.2;0;0.08;0;0|0.08;0.08;0;0;0;0,true,1064,,,,,,,,,,,,,"Eckardt, Masuda, Fan & Byer, IEEE J. Quantum Electron. 26, 922 (1990) (d22=2.2); EKSMA Optics BBO datasheet 2022 rev (d31=0.08)","beta-BBO; d22 effectively wavelength-flat 800-1064 nm; d33 unpinned/negligible, stored 0; Kleinman d15=d24=d31"
chi2_tensor,ktp_d,ktp,mm2,0;0;0;0;1.9;0|0;0;0;3.5;0;0|2.2;3.9;15.3;0;0;0,false,1064,,,,,,,,,,,,,"Eckardt, Masuda, Fan & Byer, IEEE J. Quantum Electron. 26, 922 (1990) (|d15|=1.9); Kato, IEEE J. Quantum Electron. 27, 1137 (1991) (|d24|/|d15|=1.8 -> d24=3.5); EKSMA-centered vendor consensus d31=2.2 d32=3.9 d33=15.3","mm2 matrix [[0,0,0,0,d15,0],[0,0,0,d24,0,0],[d31,d32,d33,0,0,0]]; KTP measurably VIOLATES Kleinman (d15!=d31, d24!=d32; likely primary Bierlein & Vanherzeele, JOSA B 6, 622 (1989)) so measured d15/d24 are stored, not d31/d32 copies; ~25% genuine literature scatter on d31/d32/d33"
chi2_tensor,lbo_d,lbo,mm2,0;0;0;0;1.05;0|0;0;0;-0.98;0;0|1.05;-0.98;0.05;0;0;0,true,1064,,,,,,,,,,,,,"Velsko, Webb, Davis & Huang, IEEE J. Quantum Electron. 27, 2182 (1991) (d31=1.05, d32=-0.98, d33=0.05; Eckardt/Byer absolute scale)","mm2; obeys Kleinman well (d15=d31, d24=d32), unlike KTP; discovery-paper (Lin et al. 1990) values use a different axis convention -- these are the Velsko recalibration everyone quotes"
chi2_tensor,kdp_d,kdp,-42m,0;0;0;0.38;0;0|0;0;0;0;0.38;0|0;0;0;0;0;0.38,true,1064,,,,,,,,,,,,,"Eckardt, Masuda, Fan & Byer, IEEE J. Quantum Electron. 26, 922 (1990) (d36=0.38 pm/V, direct SHG; anchor of the modern absolute scale)","-42m matrix [[0,0,0,d14,0,0],[0,0,0,0,d25,0],[0,0,0,0,0,d36]] with d14=d25 (symmetry) = d36 (Kleinman); d36 is the only independent SHG component; KD*P: 0.37; historical spread 0.39-0.78 is pre-recalibration"
chi2_process,ktp_shg_1064_type2,ktp,,,,,shg_type2,1064,90,23.5,3.2,,,,,,,,"Eckardt & Byer, Proc. SPIE 1561, 119 (1991) Table II (d_eff=3.2 pm/V, 10%-accuracy absolute SHG measurement); phi=23.50 deg experimental phase-matching value for 1064.2->532.10 nm at 300 K (vendor stock cut theta=90 phi=23.5)","non-critical in theta (propagation in the XY principal plane); angular acceptance ~15 mrad*cm; the standard intracavity 532 nm doubler"
chi2_process,bbo_shg_800_type1,bbo,,,,,shg_type1,800,29.2,90,1.95,,,,,,,,"EKSMA Optics catalog + dmphotonics.com stock SHG@800nm type-I cuts (theta_pm=29.2 deg, phi=90); d_eff=d31*sin(theta)+d22*cos(theta)~1.95 pm/V derived from Eckardt et al. 1990 d22 + EKSMA d31","ooe in negative uniaxial beta-BBO; consistent with the primary 1064 nm measurement d_eff=1.94 pm/V at theta=22.8 (angle geometry, not dispersion of d); walk-off ~4-5 deg at 800 nm"
pockels,kdp_star_q_switch,kdp,,,,,,,,,,r63=26.4,longitudinal,,,,,,"Standard EO tables (Zernike/Midwinter lineage) r63(KD*P)=26.4 pm/V; device cross-check: Leysop/Inrad/EOC KD*P longitudinal cells quote ~6 kV V_pi at 1064 nm (= lam/(2 n_o^3 r63))","deuterated KD*P (KD2PO4); real ~10% table spread (23.6-26.4), likely deuteration-fraction dependent; index rows resolve to the plain 'kdp' crystal entry (deuteration index shift small); plain KDP r63=10.5-10.6 for context"
pockels,linbo3_eo,linbo3,,,,,,,,,,r33=30.8;r13=8.6,transverse,,,,,,"Weis & Gaylord, Appl. Phys. A 37, 191 (1985) (unclamped/low-frequency, congruent LiNbO3, 633 nm); modern stoichiometric remeasurement 30.2+-0.6 consistent","transverse geometry: V_pi ~ lam*d/(2 n_o^3 r33 L), device-specific via gap/length d/L; unclamped values include the piezoelectric contribution -- clamped (>GHz) values are smaller and NOT pinned here"
n2,n2_fused_silica,,,,,1053,,,,,,,,fused_silica,2.7e-20,,,,"D. Milam, Appl. Opt. 37, 546 (1998) critical review (recommends 2.74e-20 at 1053 nm); modern consensus 2.2-2.7e-20 with little dispersion 1-1.6 um (Vermeulen et al., J. Phys. Photonics 5, 035001 (2023))","lam_ref 1053 nm; founding Z-scan value 3.0e-20 (Sheik-Bahae et al. 1990) runs ~10% above the review recommendation"
n2,n2_sapphire,,,,,1064,,,,,,,,sapphire_o,2.9e-20,,,,"DeSalvo et al., IEEE J. Quantum Electron. 32, 1324 (1996) Z-scan survey; consistent with Major et al., Opt. Lett. 29, 602 (2004) dispersion curve (~2.8e-20 near 1064-1550 nm)","lam_ref ~1064 nm; material row is the o-ray index of uniaxial sapphire; real 30-50% cross-paper spread (alt. DeSalvo determination 2.16e-20)"
n2,n2_yag,,,,,1064,,,,,,,,yag,6.0e-20,,,,"DeSalvo et al., IEEE J. Quantum Electron. 32, 1324 (1996)","lam_ref 1064 nm, undoped YAG; NOTE: no 'yag' index row exists in materials.miemat yet (staged -- see library_data/staged/nonlinear_staging_notes.md); the material field is resolved lazily by the Kerr consumer"
n2,n2_bk7,,,,,1060,,,,,,,,bk7,3.4e-20,,,,"Adair, Chase & Payne, J. Opt. Soc. Am. B 4, 875 (1987) (27-glass three-wave-mixing survey, calibrated vs fused silica)","lam_ref ~1000-1060 nm; fs-filament value at 800 nm ~2.25e-20 (Wang et al., Appl. Opt. 51, 2045 (2012)) illustrates the pulse-regime spread; recommend the Adair table value"
saturable,sam_1550_16_2ps,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,6.0e7,0.84,2.0e-12,"BATOP GmbH SAM-1550-16-2ps datasheet (F_sat=60 uJ/cm2, low-intensity absorption A=16%, modulation depth dR=9%, non-saturable loss 7%, tau~2 ps); I_sat = F_sat/tau_pulse at tau_pulse=1 ps = 6e7 W/cm2","T0 = unsaturated REFLECTANCE 1-A=0.84 (this is a mirror device); modulation depth 0.09 and non-saturable loss 0.07 ride in this note; HR range 1480-1600 nm; I_sat is a scaling estimate tied to the 1 ps assumption (6e8 W/cm2 at 100 fs), not a rate-equation quantity"
